cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use a finding from this cookbook, please cite it."
# type is software, not dataset: the citable object here is the METHOD — a
# recipe you can re-run — not a captured corpus. The corpora live in the
# wss-* archives, which are cited separately as datasets.
type: software
title: "Data Analysis Cookbook (q3dresearch/cookbook)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible recipes that turn public records into findings. Each recipe is
  one question, one method, one figure, and a written account of what the
  answer cannot support. Companion to the wss-* archives, which capture public
  records their publishers overwrite; this holds the reasoning built on them
  and on sources that keep their own history.
authors:
  - name: "neldivad"
    website: "https://github.com/neldivad"
  - name: "q3dresearch"
    website: "https://github.com/q3dresearch"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/q3dresearch/cookbook"
